<figure class="viz" id="viz-npu">
  <p class="chart-title">Safe, predictable, unpredictable</p>
  <div class="npu">
    <div class="npu-panel">
      <p class="npu-kicker">N</p>
      <h3>Safe</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>A quiet stretch</li>
        <li>The room stays safe</li>
        <li>Startle sits at its baseline</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="npu-panel">
      <p class="npu-kicker">P</p>
      <h3>Predictable</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>A cue marks the moment</li>
        <li>You know when it will arrive</li>
        <li>The wait has an edge you can see</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="npu-panel">
      <p class="npu-kicker">U</p>
      <h3>Unpredictable</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>It can arrive at any moment</li>
        <li>The timing stays open</li>
        <li>Startle during the wait is larger</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    A sketch of the three waiting rooms in the NPU-threat test. The open-ended wait produces the bigger startle.{' '}
    <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/nprot.2012.001">Schmitz and Grillon, 2012</a>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
